<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Yes.%20a%20ECG%20morphology%20suggestive%20of%20RVOT%20or%20fascicular%20origin%2C%20negative%20family%20history%2C%20normal%2012-lead%20ECG%2C%20and%20echocardiogram.%20b%20e.g.%20atrioventricular%20conduction%20abnormalities%2C%20Q%20waves%2C%20broad%20QRS%20complex%2C%20ST%2FT%20waves%20deviations%2C%20abnormally%20high%20or%20low%20voltages.%20Ventricular%20dysfunction%2Fdilatation%2Fhypertrophy%2Fwall%20thinning%2C%20wall%20motion%20abnormalities%2C%20multitopic%20PVCs%2FNSVTs%2Fincreasing%20ventricular%20arrhythmia%20%28VA%29%20burden%20with%20exercise.%20c%20e.g.%20Brugada%20pattern%2C%20long%2Fshort%20QT%2C%20polymorphic%2Fbidirectional%20VA%20with%20exercise.%20d%20Diagnostic%20test%20to%20exclude%20CAD%20according%20to%20patient%20profile%20and%20symptoms.%20e%20Consider%20re-evaluation%20in%20case%20of%20new%20symptoms%20or%20changes%20in%20patient%20clinical%20condition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/Expansion>.
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Yes.%20a%20ECG%20morphology%20suggestive%20of%20RVOT%20or%20fascicular%20origin%2C%20negative%20family%20history%2C%20normal%2012-lead%20ECG%2C%20and%20echocardiogram.%20b%20e.g.%20atrioventricular%20conduction%20abnormalities%2C%20Q%20waves%2C%20broad%20QRS%20complex%2C%20ST%2FT%20waves%20deviations%2C%20abnormally%20high%20or%20low%20voltages.%20Ventricular%20dysfunction%2Fdilatation%2Fhypertrophy%2Fwall%20thinning%2C%20wall%20motion%20abnormalities%2C%20multitopic%20PVCs%2FNSVTs%2Fincreasing%20ventricular%20arrhythmia%20%28VA%29%20burden%20with%20exercise.%20c%20e.g.%20Brugada%20pattern%2C%20long%2Fshort%20QT%2C%20polymorphic%2Fbidirectional%20VA%20with%20exercise.%20d%20Diagnostic%20test%20to%20exclude%20CAD%20according%20to%20patient%20profile%20and%20symptoms.%20e%20Consider%20re-evaluation%20in%20case%20of%20new%20symptoms%20or%20changes%20in%20patient%20clinical%20condition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Yes. a ECG morphology suggestive of RVOT or fascicular origin, negative family history, normal 12-lead ECG, and echocardiogram. b e.g. atrioventricular conduction abnormalities, Q waves, broad QRS complex, ST/T waves deviations, abnormally high or low voltages. Ventricular dysfunction/dilatation/hypertrophy/wall thinning, wall motion abnormalities, multitopic PVCs/NSVTs/increasing ventricular arrhythmia (VA) burden with exercise. c e.g. Brugada pattern, long/short QT, polymorphic/bidirectional VA with exercise. d Diagnostic test to exclude CAD according to patient profile and symptoms. e Consider re-evaluation in case of new symptoms or changes in patient clinical condition".
